On 10/27/06, Michael <space3000@gmail.com> wrote:
> Most moder schedule management sofware is able to publish schedules
> and calendars in variety of common standards. You can publish things
> like free/busy info and stuff.
> It can be useful. Also google's calendar (and pretty much any other
> service) can be easily used for all sort of groupware needs.
> It realy shouldn't be a big deal to manage the schedules, as long as
> people are willing to take part in the schedule management.

Michael,

People are not willing to take part in schedule management, especially
when they are volunteers and they can really take it or leave it.
That's why schedule management software fails.

I've been scheduling meetings in volunteer organizations and
get-togethers in noncommitted casual social groups every week or every
month for years, and I've learned that the solution doesn't just need
technology, it needs psychology.  Please read the meetomatic "About"
page:

http://www.meetomatic.com/about.asp

-epkat


